Z||000005||84Bill||07-01-2001||09:59 PM||||How did your car make out? Did they love that hood of yours?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/op/hood.jpg"> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 07-01-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000006||skitime||07-01-2001||10:08 PM||||I couldn't believe how many Fiero people walked by and never noticed it.  Some thought it was a mirror.||||reg||1
Z||000007||MooCow||07-01-2001||10:37 PM||||Skitime how did you do that????  That is awsome looking.  Is it plexiglass??  Please give more details.<BR>Also more pics of the show if you have em.<P>                                Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000008||skitime||07-01-2001||10:48 PM||||Ken, Thanks for the compliment.  I don't have a lot of pics yet.  The window is Lexan but will be glass soon I hope.  The grills are made from GT grills so they match exactly.  Designing it and developing the concept took alot of time. The grills were designed and resigned four times. I worked with a trunk as a prototype before starting this one. I kept the original one in case I want to convert back.  So it took three trunks and two sets of GT grills to get it right. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7010024-1.JPG"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P7010022-1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||CoolBlue87GT||07-01-2001||11:09 PM||||Welcome back !!  Glad you survised.<BR>How many of them were there for Carlisle 1 ?<BR>I missed seeing that hood. Looks great !<BR>.<BR>Looks like no blue ones were there.||||reg||6
Z||000010||skitime||07-01-2001||11:13 PM||||Dave I kept looking for you. I was hoping.  We had over 105 at Carlisle I.  The trunk was finished Friday. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000011||kslish||07-02-2001||12:04 AM||||Hmmm interesting, I never expected to actually place but I guess with 12 awards and 24 cars there was 50% chance...I didn't even realize that they had three places in each class.  <P>Anyone know how many cars were in each class? <P>Since I didn't stick around for the awards on Sunday, will they mail the trophy to those that weren't present?<P>Anyways, when I wasn't sleeping in my chair (from both a lack of sleep and the crazy heat) I enjoyed talking to everyone that I met for the first time and those that I already knew.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||CoolBlue87GT||07-02-2001||12:12 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by skitime:<BR><B>Dave I kept looking for you</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I came close.  Of course, now I have the next 3 days off !! <P>Yes, the hood was a nice addition. Did you just cut between the braces ? What a neat idea.<P>||||reg||6
Z||000013||skitime||07-02-2001||12:22 AM||||Kslish - Yes, I understand that your award will be mailed to you and congratulations.<P>Dave - Three days off and you didn't come! The concept is to cut between the braces but it is not quite that simple or you would lose the strength and joint between the surface and the braces.||||reg||1
